      "writtenOn": "2017-07-13T02:52:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe I missed something but couldn\u0027t this be fixed by just setting CAPACITY_MARGIN high enough? Or is your concern for the case where CAPACITY_MARGIN is changed to be something more border-line?\n\nAlso new_util should have some idea already about the util of the task right, so if its going to run for a while, shouldn\u0027t that already be factored in?\n\nI didn\u0027t really like the addition of more magic numbers. (How could we know 10ms is the correct number, etc..)\nMaybe this can instead be a tunable set to 0 by default which can use in your testing? But I still feel IMHO that ACK should only contain mostly tested / proven stuff.",
